 "intro": "Meeting someone after a long time, asking how things are going, sending regards and saying a proper goodbye.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "cuánto tiempo",
   "significado": "long time no see",
   "pron": "KWAN-to TYEM-po",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is an exclamation: «¡cuánto tiempo!». «Cuánto» has an accent because it is exclamatory.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "me alegro de verte",
   "significado": "I am glad to see you",
   "pron": "me a-LE-gro de BER-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Alegrarse de» takes an infinitive if the subject is the same: «me alegro de verte».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "qué tal te va",
   "significado": "how are things going for you?",
   "pron": "ke TAL te ba",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is informal. «Qué tal» has an accent on «qué». You answer with «bien», «tirando» or «fenomenal».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tirando",
   "significado": "getting by",
   "pron": "ti-RAN-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «ir tirando». It is what you answer when things are so-so.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "estupendamente",
   "significado": "wonderfully",
   "pron": "es-tu-pen-da-MEN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «estupendo» plus «-mente». It is an energetic way of saying «muy bien».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cómo va lo de",
   "significado": "how is that business of… going?",
   "pron": "KO-mo ba lo de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A noun follows «lo de»: «¿cómo va lo de tu piso?». It shows you remember the subject.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "dar recuerdos",
   "significado": "to give regards",
   "pron": "dar rre-KWER-dos",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is asked like this: «dale recuerdos a tu madre». «Recuerdos» here are not memories but greetings.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "de mi parte",
   "significado": "from me, on my behalf",
   "pron": "de mi PAR-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes at the end: «dale un abrazo de mi parte». «Parte» is feminine.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "a ver si nos vemos",
   "significado": "let us see if we can meet up",
   "pron": "a ber si nos BE-mos",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is informal and often closes a goodbye. After «si» comes the indicative: «a ver si nos vemos».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "lo mismo digo",
   "significado": "the same to you, likewise",
   "pron": "lo MIS-mo DI-go",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You answer a greeting or a wish with it. The d in «digo» is a normal d, not th.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "pasárselo bien",
   "significado": "to have a good time",
   "pron": "pa-SAR-se-lo byen",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It carries «se» and «lo»: «pásatelo bien», «que te lo pases bien». It has an accent on the first a.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cruzar los dedos",
   "significado": "to cross one's fingers",
   "pron": "kru-THAR los DE-dos",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "People say «crucemos los dedos» to wish for luck. The z in «cruzar» sounds like th.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "don",
   "significado": "Mr (with a first name)",
   "pron": "don",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes with the first name: «don Ramón». For women it is «doña». It is written in lower case.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "aprovechar",
   "significado": "to make the most of",
   "pron": "a-pro-be-CHAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is a very useful verb: «aprovecha estos días». The ch sounds as in «chico».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "verte",
   "significado": "to see you (ver)",
   "pron": "BER-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The v sounds like b. «te» attaches to the infinitive.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "paja",
   "significado": "straw",
   "pron": "PA-ja",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Dry stalks used for hats and baskets. The j sounds like h.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "reconocen",
   "significado": "recognise (reconocer)",
   "pron": "rre-ko-NO-then",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "From «conocer», to know. «reconocer» means to recognise again.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "enseguida",
   "significado": "right away",
   "pron": "en-se-GI-da",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Written as one word. It means at once or immediately.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cestas",
   "significado": "baskets",
   "pron": "THES-tas",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Woven containers for carrying food. Plural of «cesta».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "interrumpen",
   "significado": "interrupt (interrumpir)",
   "pron": "in-te-RRUM-pen",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«interrumpir» means to cut in while someone speaks.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "enumera",
   "significado": "lists (enumerar)",
   "pron": "e-nu-ME-ra",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«enumerar» means to list things one by one. Here it means count.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "torre",
   "significado": "tower",
   "pron": "TO-rre",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A tall, narrow building. The double r sounds strong.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "despiden",
   "significado": "say goodbye (despedirse)",
   "pron": "des-pi-DEN",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "From «despedirse», to say goodbye. The -en ending means they.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "desear",
   "significado": "to wish (desear)",
   "pron": "de-se-AR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
